---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "Explore Stocks Through Data & Rules-Based Analysis";
const description =
  "A free technical screener and reference for Indian equity markets. Filter NSE " +
  "stocks by RSI, ADX, moving averages and volume using thresholds you set, and " +
  "learn what each indicator actually measures.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description} crumb="Introduction">
  <h1>Explore stocks through data, not opinions</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    This site computes standard technical indicators across the NSE universe each
    trading day and lets you filter them using conditions you define. It is a
    measurement and reference tool — not a tip service, and not a recommendation
    engine.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/screener/">Open the screener →</a>
  </p>

  <h2>What is here</h2>
  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card">
      <h3><a href="/screener/">Screener</a></h3>
      <p>Filter NSE stocks by indicator values. You set every threshold; the
        table recomputes as you move them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3><a href="/learn/rsi/">Technical analysis</a></h3>
      <p>What RSI, ADX, moving averages and volume measure — and, just as
        importantly, what they do not.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3><a href="/tools/cagr-calculator/">Calculators</a></h3>
      <p>CAGR, XIRR, SIP, position sizing and risk-reward. Everything runs in
        your browser; nothing is stored.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>What is not here</h2>
  <div class="defs">
    <div class="def">
      <div class="h"><code>no_buy_sell_calls</code><span class="meta">by design</span></div>
      <p>No entry prices, stop-losses or targets. Indicator values describe what
        price has already done.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="def">
      <div class="h"><code>no_predictions</code><span class="meta">by design</span></div>
      <p>No indicator forecasts future prices. Anyone claiming otherwise is
        selling something.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="def">
      <div class="h"><code>no_personalised_advice</code><span class="meta">by design</span></div>
      <p>Suitability depends on your goals, horizon and risk tolerance — none of
        which this site knows.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ad">Advertisement</div>

  <h2>Data and method</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Daily OHLCV from public sources, indicators computed with standard formulas,
    refreshed once per trading day. Where a value cannot be computed it is shown
    as unavailable rather than estimated, and every row carries the date of the
    price bar it was derived from.
    <a href="/methodology/">Read the full methodology</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Investing for the long term</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Technical screening is a short-horizon activity. If you are investing toward
    long-term goals, mutual funds are usually the more appropriate vehicle.
    <a href="/mutual-funds/">Read more</a>, or
    <a href="https://tilak004.github.io/Business_website/" rel="noopener">visit
    Shastri Financial Services</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
